  "title": "Creative tools fill the app catalog",
  "summary": "A community-heavy day added dozens of app listings, then tidied the catalog that has to hold them.\n\nAgent-added listings brought community projects for image generation, photo editing, writing, presentations, flyers, and short videos into the catalog. Examples include PixArt AI for iOS artwork, Whiskautoz for bulk images, Postify for WordPress drafts, and Pimp my Pics for photo effects. These PRs added listings, not new Pollinations API features.\n\nThe catalog gained community chat clients, social bots, and conversational tools across several languages. Listings range from Telegram and Discord bots to Pollinations AI Studio’s dialogue, image, and video client, plus InstAI’s image-sharing platform. The work makes those projects easier to discover; it does not change their underlying behavior.\n\nOther agent-added listings span decision-making games, language-learning quests, transcription, knowledge maps, and developer workflows. Among them are Lapse Game 2075, ScrollQuest, Faster Vox, community-made n8n nodes for Pollinations image and text APIs, and a console editor with LLM tools. The range is a useful reminder that an app catalog rarely stays inside its categories.",
